 "observations": [
  "col_left L4: «Nöldeke» is printed with ö. The comma after «II» is printed short (1.6 by 2.4 points, its foot 0.8 point below the baseline).",
  "col_left L12: the comma after «II» is printed short (1.7 by 2.0 points, its foot 0.6 point below the baseline), like a point at low resolution; read at 6,000 dpi. The e of «Nouet» is printed broken, its lower stroke apart like a point (1.2 by 1.4 points); it is not a point.",
  "col_left L17, L26: «nychthemerōn» and «rōn» have a bar over the o.",
  "col_left L18: a speck (1.4 by 1.4 points) in the margin before «quatio», on the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L21: a speck (0.6 by 0.6 point) above the point of «lin.», 7 points above the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L22: «al-Battānī» has bars over the second a and the last i (2.6 by 1.1 points).",
  "col_left L26: a speck (1.2 by 1.2 points) to the right of «(adn. 222).», at mid height, is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L26, L27: a blank line separates the names in N from those in O.",
  "col_left L27: «‘Obadyāh» begins with the sign of ‘ayn; «Dāwid» has a bar over the a and a dotted i (1.3 by 1.3 points).",
  "col_left L36, col_right L1, L12, L28: «figurae» (twice), «fixarum» and «perficiatur» are printed with the fi ligature.",
  "col_left L39: «οἶκοι» is Greek, read at 4,800 dpi: the ι carries the smooth breathing and the circumflex in one sort; the κ is printed in its cursive form (ϰ).",
  "col_left L42, L43: the 0 of «190», the 9 of «193» and the second 3 of «303» are printed broken; read as the figures.",
  "col_right L3, L4, L5, L6: «Omar» at the head of the first entry is printed without the sign of ‘ayn; «‘Omar» (three times) and «‘Omārah» begin with it; «Muḥ.» has the ḥ sort; «al-Farrukhān» and «‘Omārah» have their bars; «al-Khayyāmī» has bars over the a and the last i (2.3 by 1.2 points).",
  "col_right L10: a speck (0.8 by 0.7 point) above the comma after «228», 7.7 points above the baseline, is not transcribed; the mark is a comma, not a semicolon.",
  "col_right L12: the u of «quid» is printed with a mark joined to its top over the right half of the letter, which closes its opening and rises 1.0 point above the letter, like a low circumflex (the circumflex of â, p. 392, rises about 1.8 points above its letter); read u. The ball at the end of the tail of the italic 9 of «*129*» stands apart from the figure, like a point; it is not a point.",
  "col_right L14: the o of «Solis», the e and the t of «et» and the v of «v.» are printed broken; read as the letters.",
  "col_right L15: a blot (2.0 by 1.3 points) under the e of «ordines», 1.7–3.0 points below the baseline, is not transcribed; it is not a dot below.",
  "col_right L18: «*aṣl*» has the dot under the s (1.8 by 1.9 points).",
  "col_right L20: «(?)» is printed with the question mark, its point on the baseline.",
  "col_right L30, L31: a blank line separates the names in O from those in P.",
  "col_right L33: «*Pañcasiddhāntikā*» is printed with ñ and bars over both a's. A small round mark (1.0 by 1.1 points) under the foot of the i that follows the s, 1.1–2.2 points below the baseline, is not transcribed; it is smaller than the dots below of this type (1.6–1.8 points, under the s of the words aṣl in L18 and parṣūphē in L45). «Varāhamihira» has a bar over the second a.",
  "col_right L38: «παρανατέλλοντα» and «παρανατέλλοντες» are Greek, with the acute on the ε. In the second word the α after ρ and the α after ν are printed with a small spur at the top of the letter, rising 0.5 point above the other letters (the α's of the first word have none), which can be taken for an acute at low resolution; an acute of this type rises 2.6 points above the letters (on the ε of both words). The spurs are not transcribed; the word is printed with the acute on the ε in Nallino's notes (p. 312).",
  "col_right L41: «*Parāśara-siddhānta*» is printed with ś (an acute over the s) and bars over the a's.",
  "col_right L42, L43, L44: the balls of the italic 5 of «*45*» and of the 3s of «*63*» and «314» are printed apart from the figures; they are not points.",
  "col_right L45: «*parṣūphē*» has the dot under the s and bars over the u and the e (3.7 by 1.0 points). The Syriac «ܦܪܨܘܦܐ» is printed in Serto, read at 4,800 dpi: pe, rish with its dot, ṣadhe, waw, pe and a final alaph, without the plural points; in Nallino's notes (p. 312) the same word is printed «ܦܪ̈ܨܘܦܐ», with the two plural points over the rish."
 ],
